      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I just want to offer a reminder that the developers actually play VRChat. We've had multiple cores in PCs for a long time. Heck, I think the Quest 2's snapdragon xr2 has 8 cores in total.\n\nThe question these days is centered around what is in the main thread, and how easy to move stuff around. I've heard that in Unity 2019 that uncrunch of textures is on main thread, luckily I've seen a lot of avatar advise recommending against crunch for PC avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-11-23T14:51:02.698Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Apparently VRChat is mutli-threaded but the speed it runs on is based on a single core of the cpu, meaning the performance is uncanny.\n\nThat's why I (including many other players) want to have a better performance by making use of multiprocessing. That's all it is. If we get multiprocessing in the next update, we won't be constantly asking and asking for better performance. idk how it works on quest though since they kinda suck no matter the case.\n\nAnd I have yet to ask why the developers never added this.",
